---
/* The quiet tools every page carries, in one tag for BaseLayout:

   - the command palette (Palette.astro, src/scripts/palette.js)
   - previews on links to a case study, the prices or a journal post (src/scripts/peek.js)
   - sound, off until asked (src/scripts/sound.js; its switch is SoundSwitch.astro)
   - drag to dismiss on the client sheet, touch only (src/scripts/sheet-drag.js)
   - the Speculation Rules below

   Their styles are src/styles/elevate-b.css. None of it is needed to read or use a page: with no
   script the palette's buttons and the sound switch are hidden and every link is a plain link.

   Speculation Rules: in a browser that has them (Chrome and Edge today), a link to another page
   of this site is fetched ahead when the visitor shows intent ("moderate": about 200ms of hover,
   or the press itself), so the page opens at once. PREFETCH only, never prerender: a prerendered
   page would run analytics and the contact form's scripts for a visit that may never happen.
   Left out: /api/ (the contact endpoint), any address with a query string (?client=, ?print=,
   ?sent= and the like change what a page does, and each would be a second copy of the same
   file), files (anything with a dot: the feed, PDFs, this site's JSON), and links that open
   another tab or carry rel=nofollow. "/*" only ever matches this site, so other sites are out. */
import '../styles/elevate-b.css';
import Palette from './Palette.astro';

const rules = {
  prefetch: [
    {
      where: {
        and: [
          { href_matches: '/*' },
          { not: { href_matches: '/api/*' } },
          { not: { href_matches: '/*\\?*' } },
          { not: { href_matches: '/*.*' } },
          { not: { selector_matches: '[target=_blank], [rel~=nofollow], [download]' } },
        ],
      },
      eagerness: 'moderate',
    },
  ],
};
---

<Palette />
<script type="speculationrules" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(rules)} />
<script>
  // Sound first: it installs ui.cue, which the others (and every page script) call.
  import '../scripts/sound.js';
  import '../scripts/peek.js';
  import '../scripts/palette.js';
  import '../scripts/sheet-drag.js';
</script>
